From cde29ac8b18c3fb9a19c51f6dc090ae76dbe2052 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:55:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 201/206] feat: per-cascade RSM views (cascaded shadow maps
 scheme)

User-proposed and correct: instead of one shared RSM stretched to the
far cascade, every LPV cascade now owns a sun RSM view fitted to its
own volume - the texel-to-cell ratio and the caster sweep become
scale-invariant per cascade, which removes the entire class of shared-
RSM pathologies (near-cascade texel coarsening, sweep-box growth
feeding the pancake/occlusion instabilities).

- ShadowMapFrustum gains nLpvCascadeIndex; CLightEntity mounts one
  frustum per active LPV cascade (each takes a GSM slot and a cache-lod
  slot; note HMAO + two LPV cascades saturate MAX_GSM_CACHED_LODS_NUM).
- ShadowCache::InitLPVRsmFrustum/GetLPVBox are cascade-indexed; the
  shared-RSM far-sizing logic is gone.
- All RSM state in the renderer (color/normal/depth targets, matrices,
  texel size, re-render gating) moved into SCascade and routed per
  frustum; the RSM pass pool holds two passes; each cascade re-renders
  on its own camera anchor (the far cascade's bigger cells re-render
  less often).

